Š
Nuoc Ba Lan xa hoi chu nghia nhung nam 1950, ngheo nan va phong be, phong vien tre Kapuscinski chi co mot ao uoc duy nhat: duoc buoc sang ben kia bien gioi. Va khao khat ay dot ngot tro thanh hien thuc khi mot nam sau, Kapuscinski duoc tong bien tap cu di cong can tai An Do, qua tang len duong khong gi khac la tap Su ky cua Herodotus.
Du Hanh Cung Herodotus la cuon sach ke ve nhung ngay dau trong nghe phong vien cua Kapuscinski, khi lan dau tien ong duoc cu ra nuoc ngoai, sang An Do, Trung Quoc, roi sau do la chau Phi. Cam tren tay quyen sach cau su gia Hi Lap Herodotus viet ra tu hai ngan nam truoc, nguoi phong vien tung co thoi gian la thong tin vien nuoc ngoai duy nhat cua Thong tan xa Ba Lan PAP da vao nghe va hoc khong chi cach viet bao, cach quan sat xa hoi, ma ve sau nay la cach ca nghien cuu ma Kapuscinski goi la dieu tra lich su.
"Ban co the doc voi, luot qua, nhay coc hay bo doan mot cuon sach nao do, nhung xin dung lam vay voi Du hanh cung Herodotus. Boi nhu vay, nghia la ban da tu khep lai truoc mat minh mot canh cua doc dao mo ra the gioi, da rut ngan mot con duong ma ke ham hieu biet can di, da gop phan lang quen mot su gia can duoc hoi sinh, va nhat la, da tu dap tat khao khat ban nang va chay bong trong moi con nguoi: khao khat duoc xe dich va kham pha!""™
–Hogom 100 bai, da phan tap hop tu cac tap tho truoc do, it bai moi sang tac nam 2010. Theo loi nha tho 30 tuoi, ten tap tho nghe la nay do Cong ty Nha Nam chon. Ho ngau hung chon trung mot so bai tam dac, tu cac tap gui den: Le gian don, Moi quoc gia mot thanh pho cua the gioi."ž
›Nuoc Dai Nam Doi Dien Voi Phap Va Trung Hoa la mot luan an tien si duoc bao ve tu nam 1982 tai Dai hoc Paris va la mot trong so it tai lieu nghien cuu cua mot su gia nuoc ngoai ve giai doan 1847 - 1885 cua Viet Nam.
Khac voi nhung cuon sach da tung nhin Viet Nam theo con mat nguoi nuoc ngoai, Tshuboi da co gang tim hieu Viet Nam tu nhung cau tao co ban va lich su lau dai trong quy luat van dong va phat trien cua xa hoi. Chinh vi vay, Nuoc Dai Nam Doi Dien Voi Phap Va Trung Hoa hoi tu day du nhung yeu to cua mot cuon su ky, mot cuon tieu thuyet lich su, mot cong trinh nghien cuu khoa hoc. Nhung phan tich chat che, tinh te va day tinh thuyet phuc da lam nen su sinh dong, cu the cua tung cai ten, tung con nguoi duoc nhac den vo so lan trong lich su: vua Tu Duc, dai tuong Le Dinh Duong, tuong Nguyen Tri Phuong,... cung nhung tran thua, nhung manh dat, nhung ton that va ca nhung that bai tat yeu.
Nuoc Dai Nam Doi Dien Voi Phap Va Trung Hoa la mot cach nhin doc dao ve mot giai doan nghiem trong nhat trong so phan ton vong cua cac dan toc phuong Dong khi phai doi mat voi mot the gioi truoc do hoan toan xa la: phuong Tay. Gia tri cua cuon sach khong chi dung lai o muc su lieu boi ngay bay gio, lich su van dang xoay chuyen trong qua trinh "toan cau hoa", va Viet Nam lai doi mat voi mot cuoc chien moi, cuoc chien de giu lay ban sac va linh hon dan toc. Va cuoc chien nay, thang hay bai, van la cach chung ta doi mat voi no."¯	
¬	Ten cua cuon tieu thuyet mong viet boi mot trong nhung nha van duong dai vi dai nhat nuoc My nay duoc dat theo ten mot vo kich du ngon khuyet danh tu the ky muoi lam. Nhung khong han nhu vo kich ay, Nguoi pham cua thoi hien dai nay la mot nghe si thi truong lam viec cho mot hang quang cao o New York, voi ba cuoc hon nhan that bai, ba nguoi vo hoan toan khac nhau, hai dua con trai cam ghet ong, mot co con gai yeu thuong ong het muc, mot tuoi tre song dong theo sau do la cuoc vat lon dai dang voi benh tat va tuoi gia duoi hinh hai vo so lan phau thuat, sau ong stent va may khu rung tim. Philip Roth da lan theo so phan cua Nguoi pham nay tu lan cham tran choang vang voi cai chet tren bo bien New Jersey em dem thoi tho au toi nhung nam thang sau nay, khi ong chung kien su lui tan cua sinh menh o nhung nguoi cung thoi minh, su huy hoai cua suc khoe ban than, va ca long tu tin cung niem hy vong van thuong di kem suc khoe ay. Thong qua nguoi dan ong khong mang ten nay, Philip Roth da ke mot cau chuyen vua rieng tu vua pho quat ve doi nguoi, ve mat mat, ve toi loi, ve an han, ve noi so hai, ve long ham song va can dam vo song cua con nguoi trong hanh trinh di toi dich cuoi cua so phan."Ã
ÀMurakami Haruki la tac gia Nhat Ban co khuynh huong phan khang doi voi truyen thong. Tac pham Haruki dac sac ca trong the loai truyen dai lan truyen ngan. Chinh tac gia cho biet khong dac biet chu trong hay ua chuong the loai nao hon. Nhieu truyen ngan cua ong da tro thanh hat giong duoc khai phat thanh truyen dai thanh cong, va nhieu truyen dai da chia nhanh phat trien thanh nhung truyen ngan dac sac.
Cac truyen ngan trong cuon sach nay duoc dich tu Tuyen tap Kangaruu Biyori.
Nhung truyen ngan nay tieu bieu kha day du cho tinh da dang ve de tai va but phap cua tac gia."È
ÅMysterious and frightening yet tender, these eight stories reveal the power and danger of the human imagination. All are fueled by a conviction that what moves people most are the secret and personal worlds--the interior designs--we all carry within, and that our most intense adventures are the ones we invent for ourselves."Ô
ÑLike author Linda Le, the young woman who narrates this novel is from Vietnam and is a writer, a "dirty foreigner writing in French." The narrator has distanced herself not only from Vietnamese society but also from her family. Her story is an exercise in clear-eyed fury revealing three generations of a cursed family. The grandfather was a lunatic the family locked away and declared dead to avoid shame; the father is a failed artist and humiliated cuckold; the mother is a simpering beauty consumed with lust; the uncle is declared insane because of his incestuous love for his sister, who hanged herself. The narrator, on the verge of a profound depression ever since her mother told her she was illegitimate, alternates her story with her uncle's journal. In an acid style burning with compressed lyricism and savage irony, these parallel monologues sketch misfortune's family tree. Linda Le, who traveled at age fourteen from Saigon to France with a wave of "boat people," is one of the leading young novelists on France's brave new literary scene. Slanderis Le's fifth--and most celebrated--novel."ý
úUnfolding in the tense years of the Cultural Revolution (1966-1976), Trees Without Windtakes place in a remote Shanxi village in which a rare affliction has left the residents physically stunted. Director Liu, an older revolutionary and local commune head, becomes embroiled in a power struggle with Zhang Weiguo, a young ideologue who believes he is the model of a true revolutionary. Complicating matters is a woman named Nuanyu, who, like Zhang Weiguo and Director Liu, is an outsider untouched by the village's disease. "Wedded" to all of the male villagers, Nuanyu lives a polyandrous lifestyle based on necessity and at odds with the puritanical idealism of the Cultural Revolution.
The deformed villagers, representing the manipulated masses of China, become pawns in the Party representatives' factional infighting. Director Liu and Zhang Weiguo's explosive tug-of-war is part of a larger battle among politics, self-interest, and passion gripping a world undone by ideological extremism. A collectively told narrative powered by distinctive subjectivities, Trees Without Windis a milestone in the fictional treatment of a horrific event."	®Gáz@"	)\Âõ(@"	R¸…ëQ
